{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the children struggled together within her, etc.</b> This struggling was that when she passed by the entrance of the house of study of Shem and Eber, Jacob struggled to go out and Esau held him back; and when she passed by the entrance of idol worship, Esau struggled to go out and Jacob held him back. And she thought the matter was not so, but rather that there was one child in her womb who wanted to go out — sometimes toward the entrances of houses of study, sometimes toward the entrance of idol worship — and if so, heaven forbid, perhaps there are two domains. Therefore she said, 'Why then am I thus?' — for I am like the other women who worship idolatry, and what advantage do I have over them if, heaven forbid, there are two domains. Therefore 'she went to inquire of HaShem' — that is to say, to inquire after the actual existence of HaShem — what is it?"], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:58.192580475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}